Propose per-voice command ordering and record issues found on the way

docs/command-ordering.md is the design for fixing the play-then-command
race (a speed, stop or voice_stop sent right after a play runs before
the play's background load finishes, matches nothing, and is dropped).
It defines the guarantee (commands touching the same voice take effect
in arrival order; a slow load only delays commands for the voices it
touches; stopall/fadeall stay immediate), what each command touches,
when a command waits, failure and cancellation handling, what is not
ordered and why, and the implementation and test plan. It is marked as
a proposal: it is under adversarial review and nothing implements it
yet.

docs/bugs.md gains the out-of-scope issues found while analysing v2.1's
command semantics for the design: cache commands are not ordered
against plays and are aborted by stopall; pitch correction engages
unprimed when a cold play's load completes; voice_volume on a live
input's voice misreports that input in status; the docs call an empty
selector a silent no-op while the daemon rejects it; a play dropped by
a full audio command ring stays in its voice.

No code changes.

